# Pairs with OwnerMonotonic. The registry reports a row it declines to answer
# for as absent rather than as Indeterminate, as production did before the read
# gate's Indeterminate arm: a masked committed saga reads as InFlight, so a
# bucket it has not yet drained reads its pre-saga value.
MODULE: OwnerMonotonicMaskReportsAbsent
TARGET: OwnerMonotonic
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a masked registry row reads as absent, so an undrained committed key reverts
PERTURBS: RegistryMask

--- FIND
RegistryMask ==
    /\ dec # "none"
    /\ ~forgotten
    /\ masked' = ~masked
    /\ UNCHANGED <<alias, rmap, published, rmapR, rmapOld, row, pend, term, sp, spCopy, rz, rzShards, fence, redir, sg, bound, prepped, told, dec, forgotten, late, wDone, reacted, ackOn, lk, lt>>
--- REPLACE
RegistryMask ==
    /\ dec # "none"
    /\ ~forgotten
\* MUTATION: the masked row is reported as absent.
    /\ forgotten' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<alias, rmap, published, rmapR, rmapOld, row, pend, term, sp, spCopy, rz, rzShards, fence, redir, sg, bound, prepped, told, dec, masked, late, wDone, reacted, ackOn, lk, lt>>
--- END
